# Family A17: RabbitMQ delayed redelivery (internal/rabbit/delay).
# See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./internal/rabbit/delay
BENCH=BenchmarkRabbitDelay
REF=ttldlx
AUTO_KEY=rabbitdelay
KIND_DIM=""
# ADR-013 collects the §9 rows that need a broker and are therefore decided in
# Part B.
ADR=13
TITLE="RabbitMQ delayed redelivery: TTL+DLX queues against the delayed-message plugin (A17)"
# The strategies live in the root module for family A15's and A32's reason:
# hack/bakeoff.sh runs one `go test` in PKG from the repository root, and a
# root-module `go test` cannot reach a nested driver module.
# A delay plan is arithmetic over durations and names, so
# the arms are measured exactly as the driver runs them.

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="delay accuracy; broker CPU; queue count growth -> plugin when detected, TTL+DLX fallback"
# MATRIX=default is the only grid: internal/rabbit/delay has no
# IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX branch. The dimension is the DELAY DISTRIBUTION, which is
# what both of the arms' measurable costs vary with: one delay repeated needs
# one queue, delays drawn from the ladder need the whole ladder, and delays
# spread over three decades pay the rounding error and the queue count at once.
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="dist=fixed dist=ladder dist=uniform"
# error-ms is "delay accuracy" -- the mean milliseconds by which the granted
# delay exceeds the requested one, which is zero for an exact arm and the
# ladder's own arithmetic for the other -- and queues is "queue count growth"
# outright. hops/plan is the closest available proxy for "broker CPU": the
# number of times the broker moves a message before it is deliverable again,
# which is two for a park-and-dead-letter and one for a publication the broker
# holds itself. ns/op is what building the plan costs and is not the criterion.
DECIDED_ON="error-ms queues hops/plan ns/op"
# Broker CPU itself is not measurable in this package: it needs a broker, a
# load and a way to attribute its Erlang scheduler time to a mechanism.
# hops/plan is reported in its place and named as a proxy rather than as the
# measurement.
CRITERION_GAP="broker CPU=needs a broker under load -- hops/plan is reported here as the proxy and the mechanism is exercised for real by ./conformance/suites (make integration DRIVER=rabbitmq) against the pinned rabbitmq-delayed image"
# The family's decision rule is `rules["A17"]` in
# benchmarks/cmd/bakeoff/rules.go. §9.1 fixes the outcome independently of the
# measurement -- "plugin when detected, TTL+DLX fallback" -- so a campaign that
# finds the plugin better on every metric does NOT move Auto: the plugin is not
# part of the official RabbitMQ image, and Auto is what a caller gets by not
# choosing, so a default that assumed it would fail at open against a stock
# broker. What the campaign records is the margin a deployment without the
# plugin pays, which is why both arms are measured anyway.
